22:07:35 | INFO | 🤖 Target: Decades of authoritarian institutions, economic insecurity, rigid gender expectations, and war can shape how some people cope and communicate. They can contribute to guardedness, bluntness, emotional restraint, mistrust, or stress-related impatience. But “they harden these guys into being harsh and unfriendly” is still too deterministic. The same pressures can produce very different responses, including warmth, solidarity, patience, and a strong rejection of aggression. And not every Ukrainian man had the same Soviet upbringing or direct exposure to war; age, region, family, displacement, and personal experience differ greatly. You do not need to resolve that debate before working with him. Use your concern as a reason to be prepared, not as a conclusion about his character: - establish clear, written expectations; - communicate directly and respectfully; - set boundaries around interruptions, raised voices, or personal remarks; - take concrete warning signs seriously; - judge the relationship by his repeated actions. That is neither naïve nor dismissive of the history you and your family have observed.
